datory','false','true/false whether or not the formimportexport module MUST start when openmrs starts.  This is used to make sure that mission critical modules are always running if openmrs is running.','c6227556-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'formimportexport.parentConceptServer.batchSize','200','','7cabe72a-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'formimportexport.parentConceptServer.password','','Password to use when logging in to the parent concept server. Could be blank if the parent allows unauthenticated users to browse the concept dictionary.','7cabe7f2-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'formimportexport.parentConceptServer.url','http://192.168.12.146:8180/openmrs','','7cabe8ba-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'formimportexport.parentConceptServer.username','','Username to use when logging in to the parent concept server. Could be blank if the parent allows unauthenticated users to browse the concept dictionary.','7cabe98c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'formimportexport.started','true','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the formimportexport module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','7cabea5e-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'graph.color.absolute','rgb(20,20,20)','Color of the \'invalid\' section of numeric graphs on the patient dashboard.','016c02c8-41df-4d32-b466-a82e7e25205e'),(_binary 'graph.color.critical','rgb(200,0,0)','Color of the \'critical\' section of numeric graphs on the patient dashboard.','b27a8c0f-4ef5-4912-9f10-1d18ed06a3d7'),(_binary 'graph.color.normal','rgb(255,126,0)','Color of the \'normal\' section of numeric graphs on the patient dashboard.','c040f505-0d4c-4090-98ed-b0faa2f3698d'),(_binary 'gzip.enabled','false','Set to \'true\' to turn on OpenMRS\'s gzip filter, and have the webapp compress data before sending it to any client that supports it. Generally use this if you are running Tomcat standalone. If you are running Tomcat behind Apache, then you\'d want to use Apache to do gzip compression.','7cabeb1c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'hl7_archive.dir','hl7_archives','The default name or absolute path for the folder where to write the hl7_in_archives.','3b8ea870-3c0d-4b59-82e8-f93c6f56edf4'),(_binary 'hl7_processor.ignore_missing_patient_non_local','false','If true, hl7 messages for patients that are not found and are non-local will silently be dropped/ignored','d6f7a199-a1df-442d-b6a6-71513ba0a364'),(_binary 'htmlformentry.database_version','1.0.0','DO NOT MODIFY.  Current database version number for the htmlformentry module.','7cabebc6-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'htmlformentry.mandatory','false','true/false whether or not the htmlformentry module MUST start when openmrs starts.  This is used to make sure that mission critical modules are always running if openmrs is running.','c6227344-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'htmlformentry.started','false','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the htmlformentry module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','7cabec7a-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'htmlwidgets.started','false','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the htmlwidgets module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','7cabed2e-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'inactivity_timeout','900000',NULL,'649ce9f1-221f-48ee-86bd-eb49c6a1bb4d'),(_binary 'interface','fancy','','7cabedd8-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'last_error_reported','2009-11-27T23:51:02+02:00','','c6220a9e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'layout.address.format','general','Format in which to display the person addresses.  Valid values are general, kenya, rwanda, usa, and lesotho','7cabee82-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'layout.name.format','short','Format in which to display the person names.  Valid values are short, long','7cabef2c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'list.of.clinical.encounters.sequentially','UPDATE HIV STATUS,LAB ORDERS,SPUTUM SUBMISSION,LAB RESULTS,TB REGISTRATION,TB RECEPTION,HIV CLINIC REGISTRATION,HIV RECEPTION,VITALS,HIV STAGING,PART_FOLLOWUP,HIV CLINIC CONSULTATION,ART ADHERENCE,TREATMENT,DISPENSING','Sequential list of encounters','aa318db6-178b-11e1-9603-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'locale.allowed.list','en, es, fr, it, pt','Comma delimited list of locales allowed for use on system','7cabefe0-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'location.field.style','default','Type of widget to use for location fields','496cd759-5d99-4f35-a3c6-d41e9ab7e324'),(_binary 'log.level.openmrs','info','log level used by the logger \'org.openmrs\'. This value will override the log4j.xml value. Valid values are trace, debug, info, warn, error or fatal','7cabf08a-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'logic.database_version','1.4','DO NOT MODIFY.  Current database version number for the logic module.','535be50f-ddfe-4c6a-8cde-6529b1b6dfbb'),(_binary 'logic.default.ruleClassDirectory','logic/class','Default folder where compiled rule will be stored','22dda4fa-7dcd-429b-8535-797dc0cb4ddd'),(_binary 'logic.default.ruleJavaDirectory','logic/sources','Default folder where rule\'s java file will be stored','f3bf8dfe-2db4-463b-af86-6de645f9dc67'),(_binary 'logic.defaultTokens.conceptClasses','','When registering default tokens for logic, if you specify a comma-separated list of concept class names here, only concepts of those classes will have tokens registered. If you leave this blank, all classes will have tokens registered for their concepts.','1649af61-b992-40b0-b90d-fb1cd7a153f9'),(_binary 'logic.mandatory','false','true/false whether or not the logic module MUST start when openmrs starts.  This is used to make sure that mission critical modules are always running if openmrs is running.','64e2fdf8-084a-4e49-9a57-dbcacfd869a5'),(_binary 'logic.started','true','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the logic module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','7253626f-9469-457f-b2ff-243413d8399c'),(_binary 'mail.debug','false','true/false whether to print debugging information during mailing','7cabf134-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.default_content_type','text/plain','Content type to append to the mail messages','7cabf1de-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.from','info@openmrs.org','Email address to use as the default from address','7cabf292-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.password','test','Password for the SMTP user (if smtp_auth is enabled)','7cabf33c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_auth','false','true/false whether the smtp host requires authentication','7cabf79c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_host','localhost','SMTP host name','7cabf85a-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_port','25','SMTP port','7cabf904-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_quitwait','false','','c6224e14-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_socketFactory_class','javax.net.ssl.SSLSocketFactory','','c6224f0e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_socketFactory_fallback','false','','c6224e96-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_socketFactory_port','465','','c6224f90-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.smtp_starttls_enable','true','','c6225008-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.transport_protocol','smtp','Transport protocol for the messaging engine. Valid values: smtp','7cabf9b8-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mail.user','test','Username of the SMTP user (if smtp_auth is enabled)','7cabfa6c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.ART_identifier_type','ARV Number','Set this to the patient identifier type for the ART program','c6223820-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.DST_drug_list','DST TEST COMPONENTS','The ConceptSet containing all of the ordered drug concepts that are used as a row in a DST test, OR a list of concepts delimited by |.','c6222af6-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.DST_methods','TUBERCULOSIS DRUG SENSITIVITY TEST METHOD','The ConceptSet who\'s answers are all possible DST laboratory test methods.','c6221a48-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.DST_result_list','TUBERCULOSIS DST RESULT','ConceptSet containing all possible DST results concepts (in a DST result, the result concept gets the result, the valueCoded concept is the drug).  Can also be a list of concepts by name, delimited by |.','c6222b78-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.anatomical_locations_concept','TUBERCULOSIS SAMPLE SOURCE','The Concept question for which the answers are all possible anatomical locations from which an MDR-TB related lab sample can be taken.\r\nProbably \'sputum\'.  This must be a ConceptSet.','c6222a60-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.birt_report_list','','List all BIRT reports by name that correspond to the MDR-TB program.  Pipe delimited.','c6223208-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.culture_method_concept','TUBERCULOSIS CULTURE METHOD','The Concept question for which the answers are all possible culture methods.  This must be a ConceptSet.','c62219c6-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.culture_result_list','TUBERCULOSIS CULTURE RESULT','Concept with possible valueCoded answers that are all possible culture results.  Can also be a list of concepts by name, delimited by |.','c6222bfa-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.database_version','1.0.3','DO NOT MODIFY.  Current database version number for the mdrtb module.','c62213a4-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.discontinue_drug_order_reasons','REASON TUBERCULOSIS TREATMENT CHANGED OR STOPPED','Name of the ConceptSet that contains all of the value-coded concepts representing reasons why\r\nyou would want to discontinue a TB drug order.','c62235a0-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.dst_color_coding_green','SUSCEPTIBLE TO TUBERCULOSIS DRUG','The DST result value that will be coded with the color green (Susceptible).','c6223a1e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.dst_color_coding_red','RESISTANT TO TUBERCULOSIS DRUG','The DST result value that will be coded with the color red (Resistant).','c622399c-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.dst_color_coding_yellow','INTERMEDIATE TO TUBERCULOSIS DRUG','The DST result value that will be coded with the color yellow (Intermediate).','c6223aa0-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.first_line_drugs','FIRST-LINE TUBERCULOSIS DRUGS','Name of the ConceptSet that contains all first line Tuberculosis Treatment Drugs','c622330c-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.in_mdrtb_program_cohort_definition_id','9','The ID of the saved cohort definition for all patients in the mdr-tb program.  This is used by the forecasting requirements links on the homepage.','c6223b18-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.injectible_drugs','INJECTIBLE TUBERCULOSIS DRUGS','Name of the ConceptSet that contains all injectible Tuberculosis Treatement Drugs','c622338e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.lab_list','Unknown Location','Pipe delimited list of all labs that will be performing any tests associated with MDRTB.  These are expected to be locations in openMRS.','c6221930-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.location_list','','Pipe delimited list of all locations that you want to choose from in the add patient dialogs in the mdrtb module.  This will generally correspond to the health centers that are participating in an mdrtb program.  If blank, all openMRS locations will be displayed.','c622166a-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.max_num_bacteriologies_or_dsts_to_add_at_once','4','Expects an integer value.  Represents the maximum number of smears, cultures, or DSTs that you would ever want to add at one time \r\nfor a given sputum sample.','c6223622-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.mdrtb_default_provider','provider','This will be used to mark the default provider in MDR-TB related encounters, if none is already provided.','c6223186-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.mdrtb_drugs','TUBERCULOSIS DRUGS','Name of the ConceptSet that contains all Tuberculosis Drugs','c622328a-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.mdrtb_forms_list','','List all MDR-TB forms by name, pipe delimited.  These will appear in the form list on the MDR-TB home.','c62230f0-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.organism_type','TYPE OF ORGANISM','A concept set of possible TB culture organism types, or a | delimited list of organism concepts','c62236a4-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.other_second_line','OTHER SECOND-LINE TUBERCULOSIS DRUGS','Name of the ConceptSet that contains all other second-line Tuberculosis Treatement Drugs','c6223528-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.patient_contact_id_attribute_type','MDR-TB Patient Contact ID Number','The person attribute type corresponding to a patient contact\'s ID number.','c6223924-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.patient_identifier_type_list','','Pipe delimited list of all patient identifier types associated with the MDRTB program.','c62215a2-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.positive_culture_concepts','WEAKLY POSITIVE|STRONGLY POSITIVE|MODERATELY POSITIVE|SCANTY','These are the concepts that signify a positive bacteriology result.  Pipe delimited.','c622379e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.program_name','MDR-TB PROGRAM','MDR-TB program name.','c622149e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.quinolones','TUBERCULOSIS QUINOLONES','Name of the ConceptSet that contains all quinolones Tuberculosis Treatement Drugs','c62234a6-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.smear_method_concept','TUBERCULOSIS SMEAR MICROSCOPY METHOD','The Concept question for which the answers are all possible smear laboratory test methods.','c6221aca-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.smear_result_list','TUBERCULOSIS SMEAR RESULT','Concept with possible valueCoded answers that are all possible smear results.  Can also be a list of concepts by name, delimited by |.','c6222c7c-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.started','false','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the mdrtb module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','c622141c-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.test_result_encounter_type_DST','DST Result','This should be the name of the encounter type that you want to use for encounters wrapping DST results.','c6222cfe-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.test_result_encounter_type_bacteriology','Bacteriology Result','This should be the name of the encounter type that you want to use for encounters wrapping bacteriology (smear+culture) results.','c6222d80-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.treatment_supporter_person_attribute_type','Treatment Supporter','The person attribute type that corresponds to being a treatment supporter/acompanateur/dots worker.','c6221520-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.treatment_supporter_relationship_type','Treatment Supporter/Treatment Supportee','The relationship type used to describe the relationship from a treatment supporter (A) to a patient (B)','c6223898-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'mdrtb.webserver_port',':8080','This is meant to give you a little bit of flexibility with hosting configurations.  For tomcat, the listener port is :8080 by default.','c6223726-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'minSearchCharacters','3','Number of characters user must input before searching is started.','ee10af69-6bea-443c-8759-b60061ebdc67'),(_binary 'module_repository_folder','modules','Name of the folder in which to store the modules','7cabfb16-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'moh_site_id','701','','aa319d2e-178b-11e1-9603-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'newPatientForm.relationships','','Comma separated list of the RelationshipTypes to show on the new/short patient form.  The list is defined like \'3a, 4b, 7a\'.  The number is the RelationshipTypeId and the \'a\' vs \'b\' part is which side of the relationship is filled in by the user.','7cabfbc0-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'new_patient_form.showRelationships','false','true/false whether or not to show the relationship editor on the addPatient.htm screen','7cabfc7e-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'obs.complex_obs_dir','complex_obs','Default directory for storing complex obs.','9f7e873c-18c0-46c8-8f2d-8a84ca0f7457'),(_binary 'password_policy_enabled','true',NULL,'873a7da9-cf9a-4004-9fdb-ef70539046b9'),(_binary 'password_reset_interval','30',NULL,'b82bf1b8-8895-4b6b-9f61-406fc97f7a54'),(_binary 'patient.defaultPatientIdentifierValidator','org.openmrs.patient.impl.LuhnIdentifierValidator','This property sets the default patient identifier validator.  The default validator is only used in a handful of (mostly legacy) instances.  For example, it\'s used to generate the isValidCheckDigit calculated column and to append the string \"(default)\" to the name of the default validator on the editPatientIdentifierType form.','7cabfd32-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient.displayAttributeTypes','Birthplace','','7cabfdfa-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient.headerAttributeTypes','','A comma delimited list of PersonAttributeType names that will be shown on the patient dashboard','927cca24-0cc3-4427-abee-b006f534d9ec'),(_binary 'patient.identifierPrefix','','This property is only used if patient.identifierRegex is empty.  The string here is prepended to the sql indentifier search string.  The sql becomes \"... where identifier like \'<PREFIX><QUERY STRING><SUFFIX>\';\".  Typically this value is either a percent sign (%) or empty.','7cabfeae-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient.identifierRegex','^0*@SEARCH@([A-Z]+-[0-9])?$','A MySQL regular expression for the patient identifier search strings.  The @SEARCH@ string is replaced at runtime with the user\'s search string.  An empty regex will cause a simply \'like\' sql search to be used','7cabff6c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient.identifierSearchPattern','','If this is empty, the regex or suffix/prefix search is used.  Comma separated list of identifiers to check.  Allows for faster searching of multiple options rather than the slow regex. e.g. @SEARCH@,0@SEARCH@,@SEARCH-1@-@CHECKDIGIT@,0@SEARCH-1@-@CHECKDIGIT@ would turn a request for \"4127\" into a search for \"in (\'4127\',\'04127\',\'412-7\',\'0412-7\')\"','45a5439b-d312-4ed6-baa4-97fc8f47cd50'),(_binary 'patient.identifierSuffix','%','This property is only used if patient.identifierRegex is empty.  The string here is prepended to the sql indentifier search string.  The sql becomes \"... where identifier like \'<PREFIX><QUERY STRING><SUFFIX>\';\".  Typically this value is either a percent sign (%) or empty.','7cac0034-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient.listingAttributeTypes','','A comma delimited list of PersonAttributeType names that should be displayed for patients in _lists_','7cac00e8-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient.searchMaxResults','1000','The maximum number of results returned by patient searches','c6220b20-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient.viewingAttributeTypes','','A comma delimited list of PersonAttributeType names that should be displayed for patients when _viewing individually_','7cac0250-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patient_identifier.importantTypes','','A comma delimited list of PatientIdentifier names : PatientIdentifier locations that will be displayed on the patient dashboard.  E.g.: TRACnet ID:Rwanda,ELDID:Kenya','7cac0304-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientflags.database_version','1.1.4','DO NOT MODIFY.  Current database version number for the patientflags module.','c62277ea-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientflags.mandatory','false','true/false whether or not the patientflags module MUST start when openmrs starts.  This is used to make sure that mission critical modules are always running if openmrs is running.','c62278ee-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientflags.started','true','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the patientflags module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','c622786c-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientmatching.started','true','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the patientmatching module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','c6220bac-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.adultconceptIdsToGraph','5090,5089,5497','Ordered, comma separated list of concept ids to graph in patient summary for patients > 5 years old\r\nDefault: height (5090), weight (5089), cd4 (5497).','c6220c2e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.adultconceptIdsToWatch','12,5497','Comma delimited list of concept ids to trigger alerts for patients > 5 years old\r\nAlerts trigger when concepts are empty or have not been updated in six months.\r\nDefaults: x-ray chest (12), cd4 (5497).','c6220cb0-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.adverseEffectConceptId','1297','Adverse effect concept id. Default: 1297.','c6220d3c-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.arvDrugsConceptId','1085','ARV Drugs concept id. Default: 1085.','c6220dbe-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.childconceptIdsToGraph','5090,5089,5497','Ordered, comma separated list of concept ids to graph in patient summary. \r\nDefault: height (5090), weight (5089), cd4 (5497).','c6220e4a-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.childconceptIdsToWatch','12,730,5497,5089,5090','Comma delimited list of concept ids to trigger alerts.\r\nAlerts trigger when concepts are empty or have not been updated in one month.\r\nDefaults: x-ray chest (12), cd4 (5497), cd4% (730), weight (5089), height (5090)','c6220ec2-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.hivTestResultConceptId','2169','HIV Test concept id. Default: 2169.','c6220f44-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.labTestsConceptId','1337','Laboratory examinations construct concept id. Default: 1337.','c6220fc6-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.mandatory','false','true/false whether or not the patientsummary module MUST start when openmrs starts.  This is used to make sure that mission critical modules are always running if openmrs is running.','c622669c-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.previousDiagnosisConceptId','992','Problem list construct concept id. Default: 992.','c622103e-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.started','true','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the patientsummary module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','c62210c0-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.symptomPresentConceptId','1293','Review of symptoms on presentation concept id. Default: 1293.','c6221138-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'patientsummary.vitalSigns','5089,5090','Comma delimited list of concept ids for vital signs\r\nDefaults: weight (5089), height (5090)','c62211b0-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'person.searchMaxResults','1000','The maximum number of results returned by patient searches','7cac019c-a2f5-11e0-bcd1-544249e32ba2'),(_binary 'pihmalawihacks.started','true','DO NOT MODIFY. true/false whether or not the pihmalawihacks module has been started.  This is used to make sure modules that were running  prior to a restart are started again','c6221228-a31b-11e0-bcd1-544249e32